{% set stereo = evidence.stereo_context %}
<div class="multimedia-acoustic-summary">
<h3>Stereo channel comparison</h3>
{% if stereo.status == 'mono' %}<p>The first audio stream is mono. Channel comparison does not apply.</p>
{% elif stereo.status == 'unsupported' %}<p>The first audio stream does not have a supported two-channel layout.</p>
{% elif stereo.status == 'too_short' %}<p>The stereo input has less than one complete second of decoded audio.</p>
{% elif stereo.status == 'unavailable' %}<p>The stereo measurements could not be aligned to the recorded source clock.</p>
{% else %}
<p>Compared {{ stereo.windows | length }} complete one-second windows in the first {{ stereo.max_seconds }} seconds before mono mixing. Stereo placement, mixing and microphone position can all affect these readings. They do not contribute to the AI assessment.</p>
{% if stereo.status == 'quiet' %}<p>All measured windows fell below the {{ stereo.quiet_floor_dbfs }} dBFS review floor.</p>{% endif %}
<table class="multimedia-locator">
<thead><tr><th>Decoded range</th><th>Source timestamps (PTS)</th><th>L / R (dBFS)</th><th>Gap (dB)</th><th>Correlation</th><th>Observation</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for window in stereo.windows %}<tr>
<td>{{ window.start_sample // stereo.sample_rate }}–{{ window.end_sample // stereo.sample_rate }} s</td>
<td>{% for range in window.source_timestamp_ranges %}[{{ range.source_start_pts }}, {{ range.source_end_pts }}) at {{ range.time_base }}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
<td>{{ window.left_rms_dbfs }} / {{ window.right_rms_dbfs }}</td>
<td>{{ window.level_gap_db if window.level_gap_db is not none else '—' }}</td>
<td>{{ window.correlation if window.correlation is not none else '—' }}</td>
<td>{% if window.status == 'strong_imbalance' %}{{ window.louder_channel | capitalize }} louder{% elif window.status == 'quiet' %}Below review floor{% else %}Measured{% endif %}</td>
</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
<p class="caption">A gap of {{ stereo.strong_level_gap_db }} dB or more marks a strong difference for review. {{ stereo.silence_floor_dbfs }} dBFS represents digital silence. Correlation measures similarity between the two signals on a scale of −1 to +1.</p>
{% endif %}
<p class="caption">JSON pointer <span class="mono">/stereo_context</span>.</p>
</div>
